  ('kyber-network', 'Kyber Network', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://kyberswap.com', ARRAY['Onchain swaps via Kyber pools and RFQ-style sources']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A liquidity protocol combining AMM pools and professional liquidity to enable onchain swaps with broad asset coverage.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Elastic AMM designs (varies by product iteration)", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Hybrid AMM + RFQ liquidity", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium LP concentration and incentive-dependence risk", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-controlled fees and incentives", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (KNC)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "History includes upgrades and incentive shifts; no systemic AMM failure", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Wallets, DeFi apps, treasury swaps", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2018", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs + professional market makers", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium (hybrid design; RFQ can reduce some MEV)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Kyber DAO with core development by Kyber contributors", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Internal pricing; not a primary external oracle source", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via pools/quotes • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: product/version clarity (Kyber has evolved significantly), liquidity depth vs peers, and reliance on incentives to sustain LP participation.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing (pools) with quote-driven fills", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, long-tail ERC-20s", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active (Ethereum deployment)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines pricing via its own pools/quotes, and contributes to spot price discovery.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Medium–High (important secondary liquidity venue)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('bancor', 'Bancor', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://bancor.network', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps executed fully onchain']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "An AMM enabling single-sided liquidity provision, where LPs supply one asset and the protocol balances exposure using BNT, setting prices via onchain swaps.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Single-sided liquidity with protocol-side balancing", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Single-sided AMM with protocol-owned liquidity features", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "High reliance on BNT mechanics; Medium LP concentration risk", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-set fees and parameters", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (BNT)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Experienced stress during market downturns leading to parameter changes and redesigns", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "DAO treasuries, long-tail asset liquidity", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2017", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs (single-sided) + protocol-owned liquidity", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium–High (AMM MEV exposure; design shifts aim to mitigate LP risk rather than MEV)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Bancor DAO with Bancor contributors", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Internal pricing only; not a dominant external oracle", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: protocol-owned liquidity and insurance mechanisms introduce reflexive risk; historical changes to IL protection highlight governance and treasury exposure during stress.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves (single-asset exposure vs paired LPs)", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH pairs, long-tail ERC-20s", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active (Ethereum deployments; protocol iterations over time)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: owns swap execution, sets prices through onchain AMM trades, and contributes to spot price discovery for supported assets.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Medium–High (important historically and for single-sided liquidity design)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('shell-protocol', 'Shell Protocol', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://shellprotocol.io', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps executed onchain']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "An early multi-asset AMM exploring portfolio-style invariants for efficient swaps among baskets of correlated assets.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Portfolio-style invariant across many assets", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Multi-asset stable AMM (portfolio-style invariant)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Low current dependency; High relevance as design ancestor", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Fixed / limited parameter surface", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "Minimal / experimental governance (historical)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Limited stress history due to early deprecation", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Primarily design influence (Balancer, Curve-style thinking)", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2020", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Low–Medium (design targeted low-slippage, correlated trades)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Shell contributors / early DeFi research team", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Internal pricing only", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executed swaps onchain • YES set prices via invariant • YES non-custodial (historical context)", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Contextual value: not relevant for current liquidity, but important for understanding the evolution of basketized and stable AMM design on Ethereum.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing across multiple correlated assets", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "Stablecoins and correlated ERC-20 baskets", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Deprecated / Historical", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Included as a design-relevant DEX: executed swaps onchain and set prices via its own invariant, influencing later AMM designs.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Low (historical)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('sommelier', 'Sommelier', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'yield-structured-markets', 'https://sommelier.finance', ARRAY['Medium–High (important for active-strategy class)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "An automated strategy platform where off-chain computation actively manages on-chain vaults to optimize yield across multiple DeFi venues.", "extras": {"Capital Lockups Typically none at vault level (withdrawal constraints can exist per strategy/asset conditions; check per vault) (yearn.fi) Typically none at vault level (vault-specific withdrawal mechanics apply; verify per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Typically none at vault level; withdrawal liquidity depends on upstream positions (verify per vault/strategy) (Harvest Finance) Maturity / term-structure is intrinsic (PT/YT exist “up to maturity”) (docs.pendle.finance) Yes (fixed term) — principal locked to maturity for PT holders (Delv Documentation) Yes (fixed term/maturity) (docs.notional.finance) Often epoch-like cycles (weekly) rather than free-form “anytime” yield; check per vault/product (docs.ribbon.finance) Often term-like “bond” framing (SMART Yield bonds) (lexology.com) Typically none strict, but tranche structure can imply different risk classes and coverage mechanics; validate per tranche": "Typically none; vault-specific withdrawal constraints may apply", "Dependency Concentration Risk High upstream dependency stacking (Aave/Curve/Uni etc.); Medium governance/multisig execution concentration; Medium strategy-manager concentration (docs.yearn.fi) High upstream dependency stacking (LP farms + swap liquidity) • Medium strategy-maintainer concentration • Medium vault-level TVL concentration (docs.beefy.finance) High upstream dependency stacking • High strategy/implementation risk (vault-by-vault) • Medium governance/admin concentration risk (Harvest Finance) High dependency on supported yield-bearing collateral ecosystems; Medium governance/incentive concentration; Medium liquidity fragmentation risk across maturities (docs.pendle.finance) Medium dependency on underlying yield assets; Medium liquidity concentration risk in limited PT markets (Delv Documentation) Medium maturity liquidity concentration; Medium governance/risk-module dependency; Medium collateral/oracle valuation dependency (openzeppelin.com) High dependency on correct upgrade/oracle/settlement surfaces; Medium dependency on options liquidity regimes (theblock.co) Very High regulatory risk concentration; High governance/ops concentration; Medium dependency on underlying venues (lexology.com) High dependency on specific integrated venues per tranche; Medium governance/upgrade concentration; Medium liquidity/exit assumptions per tranche (docs.idle.finance)": "High dependency on strategist quality & off-chain automation; Medium venue concentration", "Downstream Consumers Retail vault depositors, DAO treasuries, structured products using yTokens, integrators sourcing yield Retail depositors, DAOs/treasuries seeking autocompounded exposure, integrators embedding vault yield Retail vault users, yield allocators, integrators (where applicable) Yield traders, DAOs/treasuries locking yield, structured product builders, hedgers/speculators Fixed-rate buyers (PT), variable yield seekers (YT), structured product builders (Delv Documentation) Fixed-income users (lend/borrow), LPs in maturity pools (nTokens), structured product builders referencing onchain rate curve Retail structured-yield users; DAOs via “Ribbon Treasury” style products (where applicable) (docs.ribbon.finance) Structured product participants; yield buyers seeking bond-like exposure Treasuries/DAOs and integrators seeking risk-adjusted yield via a single integration (idle.finance)": "DAOs/treasuries, sophisticated allocators seeking active management", "Governance Model DAO governance with Multi-DAO workstreams + governance multisig execution layer (docs.yearn.fi) DAO governance (BIFI) + operational processes for strategy deployment (beefy.com) FARM governance + operational controls; docs also reference timelocks/controlled upgrades for strategy links (implementation-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Governance-driven incentives + parameter control (protocol-level) Governance/ops (protocol era-specific) Governance token (NOTE) + protocol ops Governance history + operational control surface (vault implementations + upgrades) (openzeppelin.com) DAO governance historically DAO governance": "DAO governance (strategy approvals)", "Historical Stress Behavior Battle-tested; stress typically manifests as strategy-specific losses/pauses and rapid reallocations rather than “bank-run” insolvency (validate per vault) (docs.yearn.fi) Stress manifests as upstream protocol issues, reward token volatility, or strategy/vault pauses; protocol docs emphasize autonomous contracts once deployed (operational continuity) (docs.beefy.finance) Notable exploit Oct 26, 2020 (~$24M) followed by large TVL outflows (“bank run” dynamic) (Nasdaq) Stress typically expresses as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) repricing of implied yields, not “vault insolvency” (docs.pendle.finance) Stress primarily appears as liquidity/market adoption constraints rather than protocol-driven yield failures (validate per term/market) (Delv Documentation) Stress tends to show up as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) collateral/risk parameter sensitivity rather than “strategy blowups” (docs.notional.finance) Dec 2025: legacy Ribbon DOV vaults reportedly drained (~$2.7M) after an oracle/upgrade-related issue (incident context) (theblock.co) Dec 22, 2023 SEC settlement impacted protocol operations and highlights structured-product regulatory sensitivity (lexology.com) Stress tends to surface as underlying market losses or tranche imbalance rather than “vault blowups” (evaluate per tranche/venue) (docs.idle.finance)": "Stress shows as delayed reactions or strategy underperformance rather than vault insolvency", "Launch Year 2020 (YFI fair launch July 2020; iEarn origins Feb 2020) (CoinGecko) 2020 (vaults live Oct 8, 2020; origin Sept 2020) (docs.beefy.finance) 2020 (active protocol period; major exploit Oct 26, 2020) (Nasdaq) 2021 (V1 mainnet in June 2021) (Binance) 2021 (Ethereum mainnet launch June 30, 2021) (DELV) 2020 (V1; V2 later) (The Defiant) 2021 (Theta Vault era) (openzeppelin.com) 2020–2021 era (SMART Yield bonds/pools) (CoinGecko) 2019–2020 era (protocol matured into tranche suite by 2021) (Medium)": "2021", "Leverage Usage Conditional (some strategies may use leverage; vault-specific) Conditional (strategy-dependent; commonly no explicit leverage, but can include leveraged legs depending on vault design—validate per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Usually no explicit leverage; strategy-dependent (validate per strategy) (Harvest Finance) Can be enabled at product level (leverage and structured positioning common via integrations; validate per market/product) Not inherent; depends on integrations Can be used implicitly via borrowing/lending; leverage exists at user level (collateralized borrowing) Not inherent; users can lever externally (protocol itself primarily structures strategy exposure) Not inherent Generally no protocol-native leverage; users can lever externally": "Conditional (some strategies may employ leverage or delta-neutral legs; validate per vault)", "Maintaining Organization Yearn “Multi-DAO” structure: YFI holders + yTeams + Governance Multisig (execution / veto) (docs.yearn.fi) Beefy DAO (BIFI governance) + community contributors; vaults/strategies documented as autonomous smart contracts once deployed (docs.beefy.finance) Harvest contributors + FARM governance; strategy development guidance published in repo/docs (GitHub) Pendle contributors + governance (ve-style mechanics exist in protocol design; ops via core contributors) Delv / Element contributors (protocol + docs maintained by Delv) (Delv Documentation) Notional contributors + governance (NOTE; protocol ops) (Notional Finance) Ribbon / Aevo team + token governance history (structured vault system documented) (openzeppelin.com) BarnBridge DAO + founders/ops historically (structured product pools) (lexology.com) Idle DAO + contributors (product suite: Best Yield + Yield Tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "Sommelier DAO (strategy creators) + Strangelove (engineering/ops); Cosmos SDK off-chain compute coordinating Ethereum vaults", "Practitioner Validation Check YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs pass-through wrapper (Medium) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation/compounding • YES transformed yield vs passive wrapper (docs.beefy.finance) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs passive wrapper (Harvest Finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES transformed exposure (fixed/variable, duration) (docs.pendle.finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES fixed/variable exposures emerge from market structure (Delv Documentation) YES fixed/term transformation • YES programmatic market structure • PARTIAL multi-protocol dependency (more internal than Yearn/Pendle; still transforms yield) (docs.notional.finance) YES strategy transforms yield (premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) • YES automated program logic (openzeppelin.com) • YES not passive wrapper YES structured yield product using multi-protocol yield inputs (CoinGecko) • YES transforms exposure into bond/tranche form (lexology.com) YES multi-protocol strategy logic (docs.idle.finance) • YES programmatic allocation (GitHub) • YES transformed yield (tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "YES multi-protocol • YES programmatic/active • YES transformed (active risk mgmt)", "Practitioner’s Note Diligence checklist: (1) which upstream protocols the vault touches, (2) strategy upgrade/admin controls, (3) keeper dependencies, (4) withdrawal liquidity assumptions under stress, (5) smart-contract/audit coverage per vault version (v2 vs v3). (docs.yearn.fi) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy contract risk (each vault is a different strategy), (2) reward token swap-path slippage/MEV, (3) upstream protocol risk (Curve/Convex/DEX LPs), (4) chain-bridge considerations if allocating cross-chain, (5) TVL concentration by a few flagship vaults. (docs.beefy.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) per-vault strategy complexity, (2) reliance on Curve/LP mechanics (historically relevant), (3) upgrade/timelock and admin controls, (4) withdrawal assumptions under stress, (5) post-incident security posture and audits. (Least Authority) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity and implied rate curve behavior, (2) oracle/market pricing assumptions for PT/YT, (3) liquidity depth around maturity, (4) underlying yield source risk (what generates the yield), (5) incentive/governance concentration risk. (docs.pendle.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity/term risk, (2) PT discount mechanics (fixed rate only if PT bought at discount), (3) liquidity depth in PT markets, (4) underlying yield asset assumptions. (Delv Documentation) Boundary caution: Notional sits near Lending Markets. Classify here when your analysis is about rate curve / maturity markets (fCash) and yield transformation; classify in Lending when focusing on credit creation and collateral rules. (docs.notional.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy payoff under spot/vol regime shifts, (2) vault parameter/upgrade controls, (3) settlement/oracle upgrade risk, (4) liquidity/withdrawal mechanics by epoch, (5) tail-risk events (vault drains / contract issues). (theblock.co) Risk flags dominate: (1) regulatory enforcement precedent (SEC), (2) governance/ops centralization risk, (3) underlying venue concentration, (4) product run-off / deprecation risk, (5) liquidity/exit constraints for bond-like products. (lexology.com) Diligence checklist: (1) what the tranche’s underlying strategy venue is, (2) coverage mechanics (how junior absorbs losses), (3) concentration in a single underlying market, (4) oracle/venue liquidation behavior, (5) governance/upgrade controls. (docs.idle.finance)": "Diligence: (1) off-chain compute trust assumptions, (2) strategist/key-person risk, (3) governance latency vs market speed, (4) vault-specific leverage/risk limits.", "Principal Protection None (no guaranteed principal protection; depends on upstream protocols) None None None (no guaranteed principal protection; PT value depends on underlying + market discount) None (economic “fixed rate” comes from PT discount; no guarantee beyond underlying solvency) (Delv Documentation) None (protocol enforces redemption mechanics; principal depends on protocol solvency/market + collateral rules) None (strategy risk is explicit; drawdowns possible) (openzeppelin.com) Not guaranteed; product framing implies structured payoffs but depends on underlying + pool rules Conditional (Senior has built-in protection via Junior counterparty, within tranche design limits) (docs.idle.finance)": "None", "Protocol Status Active (Vaults, including V3 allocator vault architecture) (docs.yearn.fi) Active (multi-chain; Ethereum-supported vaults) (docs.beefy.finance) Active (vault/strategy architecture documented; Ethereum focus in docs) (Harvest Finance) Active Historical / reduced activity (kept for design relevance: PT/YT fixed-income design) (Delv Documentation) Active (focus here: fixed-rate yield structuring via fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Legacy structured vaults exist; operational context changed (rebrand + legacy vault incident Dec 2025) (theblock.co) Constrained / high regulatory risk (SEC settlement Dec 2023 on SMART Yield) (lexology.com) Active": "Active (Ethereum vaults + off-chain automation)", "Reason for Inclusion Fits criteria: abstracts/aggregates yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, transforms exposure via vault strategy logic (not a single primitive). (Medium) Fits criteria: abstracts yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, and transforms exposure via automated compounding/position management. (docs.beefy.finance) Fits criteria: programmatic strategy logic deploying capital across multiple protocols; transformed yield exposure via autocompounding and strategy routing. (Harvest Finance) Fits criteria: transforms yield exposure (fixed/variable) and depends on multi-protocol yield sources + programmatic tokenization/market logic. (docs.pendle.finance) Fits criteria: transformed yield exposure via PT/YT engineering and multi-protocol yield inputs; included explicitly as historical/design-relevant. (Delv Documentation) Included only for the yield-structuring component: it transforms yield into a term structure (fixed-rate markets) rather than simply sourcing yield from one primitive. (docs.notional.finance) Fits criteria: yield is engineered and transformed via strategy logic (options-selling) rather than sourced from a single primitive. (docs.ribbon.finance) Fits criteria: yield depends on multi-protocol aggregation and structured payoff logic, not a single primitive. (CoinGecko) Fits criteria: abstracts yield across protocols and transforms exposure via tranching (risk-adjusted yield products). (docs.idle.finance)": "Fits criteria: yield depends on multi-protocol strategy logic with programmatic, active management and transformed exposure.", "Rebalancing Logic Strategy-defined (periodic + event-driven; allocator discretion in V3) (docs.yearn.fi) Event-driven/periodic compounding via harvest() workflows in strategies (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy-defined harvesting/compounding cycles (periodic + event-driven) (Harvest Finance) Market-driven; maturity-based lifecycle (PT/YT converge to maturity; AMM liquidity + solver/LP behavior) (docs.pendle.finance) Maturity-driven; PT redemption at term, YT captures differential yield (Delv Documentation) Maturity-based: fCash redeems at face value at maturity; trading implies fixed rate (docs.notional.finance) Periodic (weekly options cycles) (docs.ribbon.finance) Term-/pool-structure driven (bond-like) Periodic / event-driven (strategy-dependent)": "Event-driven + periodic (off-chain computation proposes actions; on-chain execution via governance/keepers)", "Risk Transformation Optimization + risk-adjusted routing (yield abstraction; not classic tranching by default) (Medium) Optimization (autocompounding + routing to underlying farms/LPs) (docs.beefy.finance) Optimization (routes to underlying protocols + compounds) (Harvest Finance) Duration + yield separation (turns yield into a tradable component; enables fixed-rate via PT discounting) (docs.pendle.finance) Duration transformation + yield separation (zero-coupon style via discounted PT) (Delv Documentation) Duration transformation (creates fixed-term claims, fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Volatility → yield transformation (systematically converts vol risk into premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) Risk tranching / structured finance (bonds/pools segment exposure) (lexology.com) Risk transformation (Senior/Junior tranches): senior gets protection, junior takes first loss for boosted yield (docs.idle.finance)": "Optimization + risk-managed allocation (active rebalancing, not simple compounding)", "Strategy Change Control Governance-/manager-approved strategy onboarding and parameterization (allocator vault “plug & play” with manager choice) (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy/vault additions are gated by protocol processes (strategy contracts define capital deployment logic) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy changes are controlled via protocol mechanisms (vault↔strategy linkage and upgrade controls), strategy development guided in repo/docs (GitHub) Governance/ops controls which markets/assets are supported and how incentives are allocated Admin/governance selects supported assets/terms and contract deployments Governance controls risk params/markets and upgrades (per governance processes) Strategy params and vault operations are not “set-and-forget” immutable; validate admin/upgrade controls per deployment (openzeppelin.com) Strategy/product operation and ongoing maintenance were treated as operationally controlled (per enforcement narratives) (klgates.com) Strategy integrations guided by a documented risk framework; additions/changes are governance/ops-mediated (docs.idle.finance)": "Governance-gated: strategies proposed/approved; execution parameters controlled by governance", "Strategy Management Mixed: strategy authors + vault managers; governance/ops oversight via Multi-DAO + multisig execution (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy contracts + DAO-approved strategy framework (practically: contributors maintain strategy library) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy contracts (explicitly described as defining how vault funds are used in 3rd party protocols) (Harvest Finance) Programmatic yield tokenization + AMM markets; governance directs incentives/market support Programmatic tokenization + AMM markets for PT/YT Protocol-defined market structure (maturities, fCash issuance/redemption rules) (docs.notional.finance) Automated strategy vaults (rule-based; typically weekly cadence) (docs.ribbon.finance) Protocol-defined structuring (bonds/pools) with governance/ops historically involved (klgates.com) Algorithmic allocation + productized tranche mechanics; risk framework for integrating new markets (docs.idle.finance)": "Actively managed strategies authored by approved strategists; execution automated", "Strategy Scope Multi-protocol (core design) Multi-protocol (per-vault strategies allocate into LPs/farms and reinvest rewards) (docs.beefy.finance) Multi-protocol (vault funds deployed into 3rd party protocols via strategies) (Harvest Finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield-bearing assets across DeFi) (docs.pendle.finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield assets) Primarily internal markets (Notional-native pools); upstream yield legs can include cToken-style yield for LPs (implementation-dependent) (Medium) Multi-protocol (vault logic + options infrastructure + settlement) Multi-protocol (aggregates yield from underlying venues and re-slices into structured tranches/bonds) (CoinGecko) Multi-protocol (allocates across integrated markets; tranche strategies point to underlying venues) (docs.idle.finance)": "Multi-protocol (vaults deploy across DEXs, lending, LSTs as defined per strategy)", "Underlying Yield Sources Lending (Aave/Compound), LP positions (Curve/Uni/Balancer), incentives, other DeFi yield legs (strategy-dependent) (Medium) LP fees (DEXs), lending yield (where used), incentive rewards (farm tokens), CLM where applicable (docs.beefy.finance) Lending yield, LP fees, incentive rewards (strategy-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Yield-bearing tokens (e.g., lending receipts, LSTs, incentive-bearing wrappers), rewards streams (asset-dependent) (docs.pendle.finance) Yield-bearing assets (lending receipts, LP-like yield assets depending on supported integrations) Fixed-rate lending/borrowing; LP yield from pool fees + underlying interest sources (nToken context) (Medium) Options premium (systematic selling), sometimes paired with lending/treasury products (product-dependent) (docs.ribbon.finance) Aggregated yield from “different protocols” per overviews of SMART Yield concept (CoinGecko) Lending markets / strategy venues integrated into Best Yield + Tranches (per-asset strategy) (docs.idle.finance)": "LP fees, lending yield, incentives, LST yields (strategy-dependent)", "Upstream Dependencies Lending markets, DEXs/LP venues, oracles (indirect), keeper networks, bridges/LP gauges (strategy-dependent) (Medium) DEXs (Uniswap/Curve/etc.), farm platforms (Convex-style), token swap liquidity for compounding, chain-specific infra (docs.beefy.finance) 3rd party protocols (Curve/lending/DEXs), price/liquidity conditions for safe unwinds, keeper/executor processes (Harvest Finance) Tokenization contracts (SY/PT/YT), AMM liquidity engines, underlying protocols that generate yield (lending, staking/LSTs, etc.) (docs.pendle.finance) Tokenization contracts, AMM liquidity, underlying yield sources Native liquidity pools, collateral valuation + risk modules; oracle/valuation surfaces are a key diligence item (audit trail exists) (openzeppelin.com) Options infrastructure / vault contracts; relies on settlement correctness and any price/oracle upgrade surfaces relevant to vaults (theblock.co) Underlying yield venues; governance/ops controls; legal/compliance constraints now primary practical dependency (lexology.com) Underlying lending/strategy markets (e.g., Instadapp-based strategies in examples), oracles/keepers indirectly via venues (docs.idle.finance)": "DEXs (Uniswap/Curve), lending markets, LSTs, oracles; off-chain compute layer is a critical dependency", "Yield Model Aggregated + strategy vaults (optimized yield) Aggregated + autocompounding optimizer Aggregated yield vaults + autocompounding Structured / transformed yield (separates yield vs principal; enables fixed/variable exposure via PT/YT) (docs.pendle.finance) Structured yield (splits yield-bearing assets into Principal Tokens + Yield Tokens; fixed/variable via market pricing) (Delv Documentation) Fixed / term yield via fCash pricing in native liquidity pools (docs.notional.finance) Structured yield (options-selling “theta” style) Structured / tranched yield (SMART Yield) Aggregated + risk-tranching structured yield": "Structured / automated yield strategies"}, "source_label": "Yield & Structured Markets"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();
